Chapter: GpuEffect
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceBuffer
  cites Gpu chapter LaunchConfig

 The Gpu effect marks host-side code that launches kernels and moves
 buffers. A function with Gpu in its effect row talks to the GPU but
 does not run on it. The Device effect (in DeviceEffect.codex) marks
 code that runs on the GPU itself.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect Gpu where
    kernel-launch         : KernelDescriptor, LaunchConfig, List DeviceArg -> [Gpu.Compute] Nothing
    device-buffer-alloc   : Integer -> [Gpu.Memory] DeviceBuffer
    device-buffer-from-host : List Integer -> [Gpu.Memory] DeviceBuffer
    device-buffer-to-host : DeviceBuffer -> [Gpu.Memory] List Integer
    device-buffer-free    : DeviceBuffer -> [Gpu.Memory] Nothing

